{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794816703,"nonce":"8E+VgM1oYEPUbcKYfIlqsMte9Io=","title":"Text shape clips are compared across aux spaces when rows follow them","message":"Text in content moved by rows carries its inner clip as a type-4 shape in the glyph batch's aux rows (text_clip::prepare_glyphs). NodeRows::path_from decides from which row a path clip follows by comparing the primitive's shape pointer with each slot's ambient_path, but ambient_path pointers index the dynamic batch's aux rows, not the glyph batch's. For text the comparison always differs at depth 0, so the clip follows the text's own row and every row above.\n\nThat is right for text whose own bound node is the scroll container (the common case). It is wrong for text inside a bound node (a card a motion binding moves) under a clip introduced by the page content around that node: the clip then moves with the card instead of staying with the page. Compare clip geometry for text, or record the ambient inner clip per slot in glyph space.","files":null}]}